01:38.380 --> 01:42.260
Germany - Kaiser Stadium

01:38.380 --> 01:42.260
Germany - Kaiser Stadium

01:43.150 --> 01:46.130
Today's the first significant game of the German League.

01:46.130 --> 01:51.540
After three victories and a draw, the undefeated Grünwald come to enemy territory to challenge

01:51.540 --> 01:58.910
the reigning kings, Rotburg, who have won their first four games of the season.

01:58.910 --> 02:02.240
This is a game neither team wants to lose.

02:07.420 --> 02:10.010
I can't wait to play this game!

02:10.700 --> 02:16.020
Let's make the king eat dust, Gen-san!

02:33.340 --> 02:38.140
Wakabayashi, this is where we'll settle our old scores.

02:38.870 --> 02:41.020
I won't lose, Schneider.

02:46.780 --> 02:51.900
<b>Battle Against the Rivals</b>

02:46.780 --> 02:51.900
<b>Battle Against the Rivals</b>

02:54.060 --> 02:56.300
The game starts!

02:56.300 --> 02:57.190
What!?

02:58.180 --> 03:02.530
Oh, Schneider has already taken the ball from Grünwald!

03:08.940 --> 03:10.180
He's fast!

03:10.180 --> 03:13.260
Schneider gets past his opponents one by one with his beautiful dribbling.

03:13.260 --> 03:14.380
And he's about to shoot!

03:15.380 --> 03:18.660
Wakabayashi, here's my greeting to you!

03:19.440 --> 03:21.900
It's a beautifully-taken oscillating shot!

03:26.220 --> 03:30.660
H-He stopped it! Wakabayashi caught it magnificently!

03:34.800 --> 03:37.310
So you have the time to greet people, Schneider?

03:41.660 --> 03:45.540
As for us, we're giving it our all right from the start!

03:52.340 --> 03:56.100
Wakabayashi advances to the top of the penalty area and kicks the ball far up the field.

03:56.710 --> 03:59.100
The ball is going toward Rotburg's goal!

03:59.100 --> 04:01.820
But all the attacking players are being tightly marked.

04:02.470 --> 04:05.460
No, there's one free!

04:05.460 --> 04:10.140
Kartz is running towards where the ball appears to be landing!

04:10.140 --> 04:12.780
He was able to run up without being marked!

04:12.780 --> 04:13.780
Kartz!

04:21.000 --> 04:23.940
Kartz runs right on to the ball!

04:23.940 --> 04:26.940
I'm here to do my job properly.

04:29.640 --> 04:32.460
And it's in! Goal!

04:32.460 --> 04:33.740
Well done!

04:34.750 --> 04:36.740
Grünwald scores the first goal!

04:36.740 --> 04:37.900
All right!

04:37.900 --> 04:45.060
And it's Herman Kartz putting in his deadly work,

04:45.060 --> 04:48.190
with a surprising assist from the keeper, Wakabayashi Genzo!

04:48.190 --> 04:53.260
At Rotburg, they scored a goal right at the start of the game with a magnificent counter.

04:55.880 --> 04:59.610
The reigning king, Rotburg, gave up a goal in an unexpected way.

04:59.610 --> 05:02.260
Will they be able to equalize?

05:02.780 --> 05:06.540
The real duel starts now, Schneider.

05:07.120 --> 05:08.750
It was due to my mistake.

05:08.750 --> 05:12.340
You didn't take kindly to my greeting.

05:14.180 --> 05:17.170
I even accidentally gave you a huge present on top of that.

05:17.980 --> 05:20.260
But the game is just starting.

05:20.260 --> 05:23.060
I'll be giving you a different present next time.

05:23.490 --> 05:26.060
Please accept that one, Wakabayashi.

05:26.060 --> 05:28.650
I'm talking about our storm of shots!

05:30.540 --> 05:31.780
No way!

05:35.800 --> 05:38.180
Rotburg is attacking in waves.

05:40.240 --> 05:42.660
A storm of shots is falling onto Wakabayashi!

05:42.660 --> 05:47.020
Our first goal seems to have made them serious.

05:50.410 --> 05:55.300
Wakabayashi Genzo, the super-great goalkeeper,

05:55.300 --> 05:57.020
stops, without exception, 
all of Rotburg's shots.

05:57.700 --> 06:00.020
I won't let anyone score!

06:01.190 --> 06:05.020
Wakabayashi, you're in full form, but I'll score a goal against you!

06:05.020 --> 06:07.020
It's up to you, Schneider!

06:07.020 --> 06:10.020
Oh, the pass goes up to the front and reaches Schneider!

06:10.020 --> 06:13.690
Is Karl Heinz Schneider, the "Young Emperor of Germany",

06:13.690 --> 06:17.370
the only player capable of scoring a goal against Wakabayashi?

06:18.060 --> 06:18.750
What!?

06:19.510 --> 06:22.640
Oh, there's Kartz!

06:22.640 --> 06:25.780
Kartz clears the ball aimed for Schneider!

06:25.780 --> 06:27.780
Kartz!

06:28.790 --> 06:30.780
The ball goes back to Grünwald.

06:30.780 --> 06:33.050
Grünwald attacks!

06:36.620 --> 06:43.180
Now that I've scored, I'll be focusing on marking you tightly.

06:44.700 --> 06:48.130
Oh, what's this? Kartz is changing to a tight marking.

06:48.130 --> 06:52.490
He glues himself to Schneider so that Schneider can't have the ball.

06:52.490 --> 06:57.100
Kartz, I never imagined you'd be marking me one day.

06:57.970 --> 06:59.360
You're right on that one.

06:59.360 --> 07:03.100
Back then, I would never have imagined that either, Schneider.

07:03.100 --> 07:07.050
We were the invincible Grünwald Junior Youth Team in those days.

07:10.570 --> 07:12.580
We won again!

07:12.580 --> 07:13.100
Yes.

07:13.100 --> 07:16.070
I don't see anyone being able to beat us right now.

07:16.070 --> 07:20.990
Yeah, and when we make the first team, that won't change.

07:20.990 --> 07:22.100
You're right.

07:22.100 --> 07:25.090
Together, we don't have to back down from anybody.

07:25.090 --> 07:29.800
Wakabayashi, why don't you become a German citizen

07:29.800 --> 07:33.280
and win the International Cup with us?

07:33.280 --> 07:37.620
Yeah, that would make Germany really invincible.

07:38.400 --> 07:40.020
I can't do that.

07:40.820 --> 07:41.620
Why not?

07:42.180 --> 07:50.620
I promised someone that Japan would win the International Cup.

07:51.790 --> 07:54.820
Even with you on their team, that is impossible.

07:54.820 --> 07:59.380
Japan has never even qualified for the International Cup before, after all.

08:00.160 --> 08:01.400
That's true.

08:01.400 --> 08:06.700
But the person I made the promise with believes in it even more than me.

08:06.700 --> 08:09.350
Who's that person?

08:09.850 --> 08:13.470
You'll surely hear about him in the near future.

08:13.470 --> 08:16.610
His name is Tsubasa Ohzora.

08:17.880 --> 08:21.620
I didn't believe it back then, but today,

08:21.620 --> 08:28.460
Japan — Tsubasa Ohzora's and Wakabayashi's country — is hosting the International Cup.

08:29.090 --> 08:33.380
Yeah, and even though we're teammates on the German team, we're enemies here.

08:33.380 --> 08:36.130
That's the reality, Schneider.

08:36.520 --> 08:37.550
Kartz...

08:38.710 --> 08:43.010
You wandered a little too far down memory lane.

08:43.010 --> 08:43.980
What!?

08:46.780 --> 08:49.620
Want to see who's the fastest, Kartz?

08:50.070 --> 08:52.660
Interesting. I accept your challenge.

08:58.930 --> 09:02.860
Stefan Levin, from Rotburg, advances by dribbling!

09:02.860 --> 09:04.420
Levin!

09:05.660 --> 09:07.140
Center the ball in front of the goal!

09:07.900 --> 09:08.660
What!?

09:09.380 --> 09:10.850
I'm trusting you on this one!

09:10.850 --> 09:11.530
Here I go!

09:11.530 --> 09:12.380
Hey!

09:12.380 --> 09:16.900
Kartz and Schneider rush towards Levin's cross!

09:19.340 --> 09:23.180
Have you forgotten about my powerful legs?

09:27.140 --> 09:27.980
What!?

09:27.980 --> 09:29.450
I'm sorry, Kartz.

09:29.450 --> 09:33.780
I now have the necessary speed for a goal scorer.

09:34.820 --> 09:36.780
He's gotten even faster!

09:36.800 --> 09:38.500
Gen-san, please stop him!

09:38.500 --> 09:44.020
Schneider makes a beeline towards Grünwald's goal, and Kartz can't keep up with him!

09:44.370 --> 09:45.750
Bring it on, Schneider!

09:46.980 --> 09:49.620
He prepares to shoot from there!

09:49.620 --> 09:53.860
He's shooting with his left foot even though he's right-footed? I'll stop it!

09:53.860 --> 09:59.330
I've improved my shooting in order to become the number one goal scorer in the world.

09:59.330 --> 10:00.780
I'll score!

10:01.980 --> 10:03.020
Over there?

10:04.160 --> 10:06.260
The shot flies towards the right corner.

10:06.260 --> 10:07.500
It's going upwards!

10:07.500 --> 10:10.500
Wakabayashi reacts!

10:10.500 --> 10:13.260
But only one hand is not enough to catch it!

10:13.260 --> 10:15.460
That loose ball is mine!

10:18.300 --> 10:19.900
I'll score!

10:21.900 --> 10:22.900
What?

10:23.530 --> 10:26.380
Wakabayashi blocks and saves!

10:26.380 --> 10:29.820
Sho doesn't stop and goes straight into Wakabayashi!

10:29.820 --> 10:32.430
They both fly into the goal post!

10:32.430 --> 10:34.700
Oh, this is deemed a foul.

10:34.700 --> 10:36.220
Gen-san!

10:36.860 --> 10:38.300
Gen-san, are you all right?

10:38.790 --> 10:41.500
Yeah, I am.

10:42.090 --> 10:45.030
The goal post is a goalkeeper's best friend.

10:45.030 --> 10:47.020
It doesn't hurt at all.

10:50.020 --> 10:54.260
What a fabulous, perfect defense!

10:54.260 --> 10:58.980
This man can truly aim to become the best goalkeeper of the world.

10:58.980 --> 11:02.020
With his abilities, Wakabayashi Genzo certainly deserves it.

11:02.780 --> 11:06.020
And here's the whistle for the end of the first half.

11:06.750 --> 11:11.020
Rotburg, who were aiming for an unbeaten streak like last year,

11:11.020 --> 11:16.370
have let in one goal at home during the first minutes without being able to equalize.

11:17.540 --> 11:21.060
That Schneider has practiced a lot.

11:21.630 --> 11:24.060
Let's be careful of him during the second half.

11:24.910 --> 11:25.970
Yeah.

11:29.510 --> 11:31.950
That's just like you, Wakabayashi.

11:31.950 --> 11:34.060
But I've got a strategy...

11:34.080 --> 11:38.840
a strategy to score a goal against you even though you're in your best form.

11:44.730 --> 11:48.100
The players from both teams are coming onto the field.

11:48.550 --> 11:51.100
The second half will begin shortly.

11:52.900 --> 11:57.560
How can they look that assured even though they're losing?

12:04.450 --> 12:06.500
T-This is...

12:07.240 --> 12:08.860
They've changed strategies?

12:11.090 --> 12:16.940
Rotburg attempts to pierce Grünwald's defense with a fluid passing game.

12:17.310 --> 12:21.820
This passing strategy will make it possible to score a goal against Wakabayashi.

12:31.230 --> 12:33.940
The ball goes from the left to the right side of the field.

12:34.700 --> 12:35.860
What?

12:37.620 --> 12:40.100
The goalkeeper is badly positioned!

12:40.120 --> 12:41.020
There!

12:41.020 --> 12:42.220
Damn!

12:42.740 --> 12:46.740
Wakabayashi barely manages to clear the ball with his hand!

12:52.450 --> 12:57.340
Rotburg now has a corner kick. Grünwald is still in danger.

12:59.400 --> 13:01.180
What are you going to do, Kartz?

13:01.180 --> 13:07.000
Rotburg can score against Wakabayashi, even without me.

13:07.700 --> 13:09.220
Shut up!

13:10.270 --> 13:12.820
Oh, what's this? It's a short corner!

13:12.820 --> 13:14.080
Not good!

13:18.700 --> 13:22.140
Levin's taking a quick shot from an awkward angle!

13:23.830 --> 13:25.290
Oh, he passes!

13:25.290 --> 13:27.620
And Sho runs to receive the ball.

13:27.620 --> 13:28.660
Over there?

13:29.060 --> 13:30.660
This time, Sho is preparing to shoot!

13:30.660 --> 13:32.060
I will stop you!

13:33.100 --> 13:34.820
No, it's another pass!

13:34.820 --> 13:36.290
The ball goes to the left.

13:36.910 --> 13:40.950
It's Schneider, free from his marker, who takes the loose ball!

13:39.060 --> 13:40.130
No!

13:40.130 --> 13:40.950
Yes!

13:47.780 --> 13:49.340
It's in!

13:49.340 --> 13:52.820
Schneider finally scores the equalizing goal!

13:55.700 --> 13:57.780
You shouldn't feel ashamed, Wakabayashi.

13:57.780 --> 14:03.780
No goalkeeper in the world could've stopped that shot, especially after that passing game.

14:03.780 --> 14:05.730
Sorry, Gen-san.

14:05.730 --> 14:09.300
It's my fault since I let Schneider free.

14:11.720 --> 14:13.780
Come on, guys. We're only just starting this.

14:14.140 --> 14:17.140
They've only tied the game.

14:18.660 --> 14:20.540
We still haven't lost.

14:21.250 --> 14:23.390
The real game starts now!

14:26.060 --> 14:27.130
Gen-san...

14:28.510 --> 14:33.360
Tsubasa, if you were here, you'd say the same thing.

14:33.360 --> 14:37.140
Oh, Grünwald is making some changes.

14:36.450 --> 14:37.140
What?

14:37.730 --> 14:39.580
They're substituting two players.

14:40.710 --> 14:46.100
The substitutes will mark Sho and Levin.

14:46.100 --> 14:50.110
Grünwald is planning to finish this game with a draw.

14:52.310 --> 14:56.100
Can the team hang onto the draw until the final whistle?

15:04.780 --> 15:05.740
Damn it!

15:06.210 --> 15:08.410
Finishing the game with this score is a joke!

15:08.410 --> 15:11.260
Soccer is about scoring goals!

15:13.130 --> 15:18.100
As a result of tighter marking, Grünwald blocks Rotburg's passing game.

15:19.140 --> 15:20.910
Minba, center the ball!

15:20.910 --> 15:21.940
I'll score!

15:26.420 --> 15:28.350
You won't get the ball!

15:28.350 --> 15:31.200
I won't lose a game against wimps!

15:31.200 --> 15:32.580
What!?

15:37.660 --> 15:39.420
Wakabayashi punches!

15:40.240 --> 15:44.860
He reacted at the right time. The defense keeps up.

15:49.010 --> 15:53.290
Grünwald gets the ball and clears it far away.

15:53.290 --> 15:55.420
The ball is outside the touch line.

15:55.420 --> 15:57.220
This is boring soccer.

15:58.500 --> 16:05.980
Wakabayashi, I was looking forward to this game so much, and it turns into this.

16:06.670 --> 16:08.220
I'm really upset.

16:14.100 --> 16:14.900
Kartz!

16:14.900 --> 16:19.140
Schneider, you're talking too much today!

16:19.610 --> 16:24.420
We don't want to run away like cowards playing soccer like this, either!

16:24.420 --> 16:25.800
Stop it, Kartz!

16:25.800 --> 16:27.140
Let go of me, Gen-san!

16:27.140 --> 16:36.380
Schneider! You always play in your own little bubble, so you're in no position to criticize us!

16:36.380 --> 16:37.990
Stop, Kartz!

16:37.990 --> 16:40.140
I understand how you feel, but calm down!

16:41.440 --> 16:43.140
A red card!

16:44.030 --> 16:46.080
Kartz is being sent off!

16:46.790 --> 16:48.530
I'm fine now...

16:51.630 --> 16:53.660
Sorry, Gen-san.

16:54.540 --> 16:55.900
Kartz...

17:02.650 --> 17:07.190
We simply loved soccer.

17:07.190 --> 17:11.510
We were always the last ones left on the practice field chasing balls.

17:12.850 --> 17:17.490
During that period, I really loved soccer and had fun with it.

17:18.900 --> 17:22.580
Can't we go back to that?

17:22.580 --> 17:25.900
Isn't it possible to play soccer while having fun?

17:31.670 --> 17:36.880
There is little time left in this emotional German League game.

17:39.990 --> 17:44.370
Gen-san, I'm sorry for the trouble I caused our team.

17:45.450 --> 17:46.760
Don't give up!

17:46.760 --> 17:49.420
Let's show them Grünwald's spirit!

17:49.420 --> 17:50.940
Yeah!

17:53.610 --> 17:56.100
We're now entering added time,

17:56.100 --> 17:58.740
and there's only two minutes left!

18:01.060 --> 18:03.220
Grünwald completely blocks out all the shots.

18:03.220 --> 18:06.460
But with nobody marking him, Schneider takes the ball.

18:06.460 --> 18:09.530
He's preparing to shoot from outside of the penalty area!

18:10.980 --> 18:15.070
Wakabayashi, I'll score by shooting from outside the penalty area

18:15.070 --> 18:18.780
to prove I'm the best goal scorer in the world!

18:18.780 --> 18:22.730
Schneider, we might not be able to go back,

18:22.730 --> 18:25.700
but I can say that I still...

18:42.760 --> 18:46.820
Yes, I still love playing soccer!

18:47.190 --> 18:49.820
Wakabayashi stopped it!

18:49.820 --> 18:52.820
He completely stopped Schneider's Fire Shot!

18:54.290 --> 18:55.340
Let's go for it!

18:56.030 --> 18:58.580
Wakabayashi kicks the ball far up the field!

18:58.580 --> 19:02.510
The ball is heading towards one of Grünwald's forwards, who is unmarked!

19:02.510 --> 19:05.800
This is just like the first goal!

19:08.220 --> 19:11.010
Oh, it's a foul!

19:11.010 --> 19:14.120
Grünwald gets a free kick at an ideal spot!

19:15.540 --> 19:18.280
It's a great scoring chance for Grünwald.

19:18.280 --> 19:21.140
All of Rotburg's team are coming back to defend their goal.

19:25.900 --> 19:26.860
What?

19:26.860 --> 19:28.020
Out of there!

19:30.300 --> 19:37.220
Wakabayashi, the keeper, has gone away from his goal to shoot the free kick!

19:37.870 --> 19:41.200
We're not fine with a tied game, are we, Kartz?

19:41.200 --> 19:45.700
We've come here to beat Rotburg, the king of the league.

19:45.700 --> 19:47.820
I will score this deciding goal!

19:47.820 --> 19:49.460
Get in!

19:53.740 --> 19:54.900
That's no good!

19:54.920 --> 19:56.340
Get back, Gen-san!

19:57.340 --> 19:59.140
The ball has been cleared!

20:00.270 --> 20:03.140
And Schneider is hunting for the ball.

20:03.140 --> 20:06.230
Wakabayashi is getting back to his goal as fast as possible.

20:08.660 --> 20:10.030
Shit!

20:10.550 --> 20:13.910
Schneider gets the ball right before the touch line.

20:16.550 --> 20:19.460
And shoots from super-long distance!

20:19.460 --> 20:21.630
I'll never give up!

20:21.630 --> 20:23.070
I'll stop it!

20:31.170 --> 20:34.560
It's in! It's a goal!

20:34.560 --> 20:39.810
Wakabayashi can't reach the ball, and it ends up in Grünwald's goal.

20:39.810 --> 20:42.490
Rotburg takes the lead!

20:44.230 --> 20:47.500
And so, the game ends.

20:52.020 --> 20:57.020
Of course, it was the ace, Karl-Heinz Schneider,

20:57.020 --> 21:00.810
who turned the tables around during the added time of the second half.

21:10.130 --> 21:14.540
You saved my Fire Shot at the end and wanted to win all the way through the game, Wakabayashi.

21:15.140 --> 21:20.100
To me, you're my eternal rival, after all.

21:21.230 --> 21:23.820
Let's quickly go to the infirmary.

21:31.610 --> 21:33.100
That's just like Gen-san.

21:33.560 --> 21:36.870
Wakabayashi wanted to win so badly that he left his own goal.

